{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception-action loop, separating sensing (obstacle events) and actuation (motion commands). The specification enforces safe, coverage-oriented exploration: random_walk is used in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and recovery states use directed turns or, as a last resort, full_rotate. All obstacle events force a conservative turn before returning to exploration. The design avoids oscillations and infinite controllable loops, and ensures steady progress while reliably avoiding collisions.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for sensing and actuation, with all events explicit and deterministic.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, progress-oriented exploration: random_walk in clear, move_forward in commit, directed turns in recovery, and full_rotate only after repeated blockages."
